[[03:56:48]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8pByyWP7RE&t=14208s) item 34, the resolution attempting to overrule your own planning commission's disapproval of the Highlands future land use map amendment. Proceeding with this overrule exposes the city of Cheyenne to a catastrophic dis- district court liability across three specific counts. Count one, the ghost project in the Topanga doctrine. Under the established

[[03:57:08]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8pByyWP7RE&t=14228s) Topanga doctrine, a governing body must legally bridge the analytical gap between the raw evidence and its ultimate decision. You cannot that gap today, which is exactly why the planning commission voted to to deny this amendment on June 1st. Microsoft's own representative, Rachel Irwin, formally admitted on the public record regarding this exact campus, Microsoft has not yet advanced detailed design for the campus. When pressed on the massive 3,000 acre scale, she confessed, "At this time, we do not have a campus of this size to pull from."

[[03:57:40]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8pByyWP7RE&t=14260s) You cannot legally override your own planning experts to authorize an industrial land conversion for a ghost project that the applicant openly admits does not exist on paper. Count two, the utilities deficit. Furthermore, your own utility experts confirm this evidentiary board void. The

[[03:57:55]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8pByyWP7RE&t=14275s) Board of Public Utilities testified on the live record that they have not been approached by this developer yet. Frank Strong explicitly confessed regarding the sewer infrastructure. It may require a lift station depending on their grading. Utilizing state statute to overrule your own planning experts to approve the largest industrial conversion in city history when the applicant and utilities admit there is no grading, no sewer plan, and no detailed design is facially arbitrary and capricious. Count three, tainted education via

[[03:58:23]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8pByyWP7RE&t=14303s) financial conflict of interest. The

[[03:58:25]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8pByyWP7RE&t=14305s) official agent pushing this massive land conversion on behalf of the developer is Brad Emmons of AVI Professional Corporation. Yet, official city records prove that this council recently utilized public tax dollars to enrich AVI with a quarter million-dollar municipal infrastructure contract. Funneling public funds to the developer's agent while simultaneously advocating their multi-billion-dollar rezoning overrule creates an egregious

[[03:58:48]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8pByyWP7RE&t=14328s) financial conflict of interest that irreparably taints this entire quasi-judicial proceeding. Overriding your own experts without substantial evidence is a fatal due process violation. Do not codify this pre-prejudicial abuse of discretion into the permanent record. I formally demand a no vote on item 34, yielding my time.

